What does a salamander have to do with US elections? Dating back centuries, gerrymandering continues to play a role in American elections today. Used more often by Republicans in the modern era of voting, Democrats have also resorted to the tactic in the past decade. But what is gerrymandering, and why is it called that? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a8ee3dee-d14a-11f1-9245-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumbnail-01-Gerrymandering.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a8ee3dee-d14a-11f1-9245-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumbnail-01-Gerrymandering.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dcbf3ec0-d14a-11f1-9017-e7dfd85b688e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:48:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French President promises 'concrete measures' in response to French students' demands</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-president-promises-concrete-measures-in-response-to-french-students-demands</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron said the government would announce “concrete measures" on Monday (October 26) to address school students’ demands after weeks of unrest. Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu was scheduled to meet with students later Monday. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3422bda-cfbf-11f1-9c62-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4AX74W.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3422bda-cfbf-11f1-9c62-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4AX74W.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63087aba-d145-11f1-bc6a-9f07d106b8ee</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:39:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Obama blasts Trump's 'chaos and cruelty' while campaigning for Democrats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-obama-blasts-trump-s-chaos-and-cruelty-while-campaigning-for-democrats</link><description>
Ten days out from the elections that will determine control of the closely divided Congress, Barack Obama took to the campaign trail to accuse the Republican president of corruption, deride his strategy for Iran and skewer the gilded aesthetic he has applied ‌to White House renovations. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7aa06634-d149-11f1-8d0a-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2b4f75ac.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7aa06634-d149-11f1-8d0a-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2b4f75ac.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cca01f20-d143-11f1-b3e4-49483962c88f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:28:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tens of thousands of Israelis living abroad expected to fly in for pivotal vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote</link><description>
Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27). Unable to vote from abroad, tens of thousands of expatriate citizens have been flying in from across the world to cast their ballots. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky met some of them at the airport.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fc43c96-d142-11f1-abf3-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-140748-141044-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fc43c96-d142-11f1-abf3-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-140748-141044-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84c0d38a-d142-11f1-9756-ef57fd2daebf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:20:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Serbia's Vucic concedes defeat to the student-led movement: What's next?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-to-the-student-led-movement-what-s-next</link><description>
Serbia's student-led protest movement won a historic victory in parliamentary ⁠election, ending the ​long rule of Aleksandar Vucic and sparking mass celebrations. But their yet-to-be named leaders face a long list of issues. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley gives us her analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/466c3472-d141-11f1-b5ca-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-140453-140748-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/466c3472-d141-11f1-b5ca-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-140453-140748-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4bb369d2-d141-11f1-951e-95345239facc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:12:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lula wins fourth term: What are the reactions in Brazil?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lula-wins-fourth-term-what-are-the-reactions-in-brazil</link><description>
Brazil's leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva was re-elected against all expectations on Sunday (October 25), but his conservative rival Flavio Bolsonaro refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to have the vote annulled. FRANCE 24's Jan Onoszko tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c5ea0e2-d145-11f1-aa19-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e357fa50.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c5ea0e2-d145-11f1-aa19-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e357fa50.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7f4c9a80-d13b-11f1-a01f-2d8c0e72d7f9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:04:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bolsonaro's refusal to concede underscores ‘serious’ challenges to Brazil's democratic institutions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-refusal-to-concede-underscores-serious-challenges-to-brazil-s-democratic-institutions</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome Dr Pedro Perfeito da Silva, Latin American specialist at the University of Exeter. For Dr Perfeito da Silva, Lula's stunning success reflects the convergence of digital organizing, grassroots mobilization, targeted socioeconomic appeals and an effective effort to mobilise opposition to the Bolsonaro political project. As he explains, Lula assembled a coalition that "not only energized his supporters but also attracted voters from groups that had been somewhat skeptical of the government in the first round."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a9e1cf2-d141-11f1-aa1e-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-130510-131145-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a9e1cf2-d141-11f1-aa1e-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-130510-131145-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">20b851f2-d141-11f1-b53e-674a2aa97c8f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:53:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will Netanyahu's security promise win him this election?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election</link><description>
Since the beginning of his political career, Benjamin Netanyahu, Israel's longest-serving prime minister, has campaigned on a promise that he is the only one who will keep the Jewish state safe. As Israelis head to the polls for their first election since the October7 Hamas attacks and the start of the war in Gaza, Netanyahu's strategy might be less effective. FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08eb65f0-ceb2-11f1-8538-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/Netanyahu-cover.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08eb65f0-ceb2-11f1-8538-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/Netanyahu-cover.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb6951b2-ceb0-11f1-b514-15a2577825cb</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:52:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Lula wins Brazil election but faces uphill battle to govern</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-lula-wins-brazil-election-but-faces-uphill-battle-to-govern</link><description>
Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's narrow election victory on Sunday has dealt a blow to Brazil's far right, but deep political divisions remain. The newly re-elected president must tackle economic and security concerns at home while navigating international tensions with US President Donald Trump.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd221fee-d13a-11f1-84ec-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4EJ8VV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd221fee-d13a-11f1-84ec-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4EJ8VV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">74f669ea-d13a-11f1-987b-63085341f19e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:38:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd221fee-d13a-11f1-84ec-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4EJ8VV.jpg">© Miguel Schincariol, AFP</source><dc:creator>Anaëlle JONAH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Belgrade in rapture as Serbian students topple Vucic in historic election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-belgrade-in-rapture-as-serbian-students-topple-vucic-in-historic-election</link><description>
Serbia's student-led movement declared victory in parliamentary elections Sunday ending 14 years in power for Aleksandar Vucic's right-wing populist party. Vucic conceded defeat less than two hours after polls closed, triggering raucous scenes in the capital as supporters of the movement celebrated the defeat of a government they blamed for deep-rooted corruption.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a18cd53e-d13a-11f1-9a7c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a18cd53e-d13a-11f1-9a7c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b51bc4d4-d13a-11f1-b6ad-09419c5f4bdb</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:19:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Live: France will maintain order without state of emergency, but it’s not off the table, Macron says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261026-live-france-will-maintain-order-without-state-of-emergency-but-it-s-not-off-the-table-macron-says</link><description>
President Emmanuel Macron on Monday said public order will be maintained in France without the need for a state of emergency, while noting that it was not “off-limits or taboo” if “things were to deteriorate". During a visit to Marseille, Macron promised "concrete" measures to address the demands by high school students after their protests triggered weeks of nationwide unrest. Follow our live blog for all the latest updates. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4904c526-d139-11f1-9ba3-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299408242327.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4904c526-d139-11f1-9ba3-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299408242327.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f78756bc-d13a-11f1-96d4-a5bd40727198</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:47:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4904c526-d139-11f1-9ba3-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299408242327.jpg">© Aurélien Morissard, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel braces for national elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-braces-for-national-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu</link><description>
Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27)  in the first elections since the October 7th attacks in 2023. Unable to vote abroad, expatriate citizens have been flying in from around the world to participate in a vote widely seen as being a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0337c57c-d128-11f1-bdd9-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-090953-091147-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0337c57c-d128-11f1-bdd9-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-090953-091147-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d77b164-d128-11f1-8057-4f90e64047c9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:35:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Football: Who will win the 2026 Ballon d'Or?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-football-who-will-win-the-2026-ballon-d-or</link><description>
The competition for this year's Ballon d'Or is tougher than ever. Who will succeed Ousmane Dembélé? Kylian Mbappé, Lamine Yamal and Harry Kane lead a star-studded field. FRANCE 24's Emily Boyle has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b137866e-ab24-11f1-9471-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-kylian.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b137866e-ab24-11f1-9471-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-kylian.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad7d6a24-d136-11f1-9252-e3fd9e083162</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:33:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron vows ‘concrete’ measures to address student demands after unrest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261026-macron-vows-concrete-measures-to-address-student-demands-after-unrest</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Monday said the government will announce "concrete and strong" measures to address the demands by high school students after their protests demanding better education conditions triggered weeks of nationwide unrest. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu is set to hold a news conference after meeting with high school student unions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0691971e-d134-11f1-baaf-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299412584753.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0691971e-d134-11f1-baaf-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299412584753.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ade564d2-d134-11f1-9bc8-6d20ccb9a352</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:25:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0691971e-d134-11f1-baaf-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299412584753.jpg">© Aurelien Morissard, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French PM meets student representatives after weeks of protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-pm-meets-student-representatives-after-weeks-of-protests</link><description>
French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu is set to meet with high school students on Monday afternoon (October 26) to ease tensions in the country after nearly a month of protests. This follows another meeting in which French president Emmanuel Macron promised a concrete response to demands for better education standards and funding.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ded243ce-d136-11f1-ab58-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5e3192ff.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ded243ce-d136-11f1-ab58-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5e3192ff.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3964036a-d135-11f1-bc1d-5187f266c5d2</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:20:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: Arab Israeli voters could prove decisive in the upcoming elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-arab-israeli-voters-could-prove-decisive-in-the-upcoming-elections</link><description>
In Israel’s election the vote of Arab Israeli citizens could be crucial for the outcome and fate of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu who is standing for re-election. Traditionally voting turnout is lower among Arab Israelis than among the rest of the population. But this time some feel it’s their duty more than ever to cast their ballot given the policies and wars undertaken by Netanyahu.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a94a6d8-d12a-11f1-83a6-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-091218-091500-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a94a6d8-d12a-11f1-83a6-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-091218-091500-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7f922ee4-d12a-11f1-9536-e32dde40c127</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:13:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>A look at the main issues in Israeli elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-a-look-at-the-main-issues-in-israeli-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu</link><description>
Israelis will vote Tuesday (October 27) in the first national elections since Hamas' Oct. 7, 2023, attack in what is widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership. He rejected ICC war crimes claims and denied corruption as national elections approach. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be013ffa-bc7e-11f1-adb1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25357403714237.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be013ffa-bc7e-11f1-adb1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25357403714237.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef307628-d131-11f1-9213-6ff749a9a215</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:59:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lula beats Bolsonaro in Brazil runoff: What does it mean for Donald Trump?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-lula-beats-bolsonaro-in-brazil-runoff-what-does-it-mean-for-donald-trump</link><description>
Lula defeated on Sunday (October 25) Flavio Bolsonaro in Brazil’s presidential election. But rather than conceding, Bolsonaro called for the result to be annulled. As the US midterms approach, the result raises questions about Trump’s influence and how his political allies respond when voters reject them. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor, Douglas Herbert, gives us his analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/407c3b70-d0e7-11f1-af1e-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277709264055-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/407c3b70-d0e7-11f1-af1e-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277709264055-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e65a7cde-d126-11f1-bca0-8f22189af98a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:50:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Trump's gains among Latino voters in Texas at risk</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-us-midterms-trump-s-gains-among-latino-voters-in-texas-at-risk</link><description>
Latino voters shifted toward Trump two years ago, helping him return to the White House with a Republican-controlled Congress. Now, many are souring on the US president and his party. FRANCE 24's team reports from the Rio Grande Valley.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c59e456-d128-11f1-ab5d-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-85a53c06.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c59e456-d128-11f1-ab5d-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-85a53c06.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0ddb751e-d128-11f1-918a-ff50aa936331</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:42:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Israeli election seen as a referendum: For or against Netanyahu?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261026-israeli-election-seen-as-a-referendum-for-or-against-netanyahu</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has led his country almost continuously for nearly 17 years. But will he manage to retain power following Tuesday's election? Netanyahu's latest term has divided Israeli society more than ever and will be marked by the October 7 attacks, his handling of the conflicts in Gaza, Iran and Lebanon, as well as his controversial judicial reform. FRANCE 24's David Gilberg reports, with Lauren Bain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0152e22a-cf05-11f1-a645-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-ISRAEL-ELEX-BIBI-BAIN-Lauren-transfer.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0152e22a-cf05-11f1-a645-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-ISRAEL-ELEX-BIBI-BAIN-Lauren-transfer.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3f13af90-cf05-11f1-b3ea-bb3c152805dc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:40:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>David GILBERG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'An everyday habit': 2.5 billion lines of cocaine snorted in England per year</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261026-an-everyday-habit-2-5-billion-lines-of-cocaine-snorted-in-england-per-year</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Monday, October 26: Brazilian and international papers react to Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's presidential election victory. Next: The New York Times warns that the war in Iran is entering a dangerous new phase. Also: cocaine consumption and cocaine-related crimes are surging across Britain. Finally, it turns out that wrapping children in cotton wool isn't the best parenting strategy.
